    id: 'oa-s0',
    mark: '0',
    title: 'Section 0. Preliminary Provisions',
    text: '0.1 Effective Date of Agreement.\n\nThe effective date of this Agreement (the "Effective Date") is the date this Agreement is executed by INTERDEPENDENT and the initial Member or Members admitted on or before the Effective Date. The Formation Date is the date the Certificate of Formation was filed with the Secretary of State as set forth in Statement of Background ¶ A. Each Member is bound by this Agreement from the date and time the Member signs it.\n\n0.2 INTERDEPENDENT\'s Name, Registered Agent, and Office.\n\nINTERDEPENDENT\'s name and the name and address of INTERDEPENDENT\'s registered agent and registered office in the State of Delaware are as set forth in the Certificate of Formation. The Executive Director may change the registered agent or the registered office at any time and shall cause the Certificate of Formation to be amended to reflect the change.\n\n0.3 Members\' Acceptance of Certificate of Formation.\n\nEach Member acknowledges having reviewed the Certificate of Formation and approves and accepts it.\n\n0.4 INTERDEPENDENT\'s Principal Place of Business.\n\n\n0.4.1 Initial Principal Place of Business.\n\nINTERDEPENDENT\'s principal place of business is initially located at 428 Route 6 West, Coudersport, Pennsylvania 16915, United States of America.\n\n0.4.2 Change of Principal Place of Business.\n\nThe Executive Director may change INTERDEPENDENT\'s principal place of business at any time and to any location, including a location outside the United States of America. The Executive Director shall cause this Agreement to be amended to reflect the change and shall promptly notify each Member of the change.\n\n0.4.3 Series Principal Place of Business.\n\nEach Series may have its own principal place of business as specified in its Certificate of Establishment, which may differ from INTERDEPENDENT\'s principal place of business. A Series principal place of business may be located in any jurisdiction, including a jurisdiction outside the United States of America.\n\n0.5 Ability to Establish Series.\n\n\n0.5.1 Establishment Authority.\n\nINTERDEPENDENT may establish one or more series of INTERDEPENDENT (each, a "Series" and collectively, the "Series"), each designated to fulfill a specific purpose, pursuant to § 18-215 of the LLC Act. The Executive Director establishes each Series in accordance with Section 2.1 and the applicable Certificate of Establishment.\n\n0.5.2 Status of Series — Default; Election of Registered Series.\n\nEach Series is a "protected series" under § 18-215(b) of the LLC Act, with the limitation of liability set forth in Section 1.8.2, unless the Executive Director elects to establish or convert a particular Series as a "registered series" under § 18-218 of the LLC Act in accordance with Section 0.5.5.\n\n0.5.3 Rights and Obligations of Associated Members.\n\nThe economic rights, authority, duties, and other rights of associated members of each Series are as set forth in the LLC Act, this Agreement, and the Certificate of Establishment of the Series.\n\n0.5.4 Series-Level Secured Financing.\n\nEach Series may enter into Series-Level Secured Financing arrangements as authorized in its Certificate of Establishment, subject to the Series-isolation framework set forth in Section 1.8.2 and the operative provisions of Section 3.13.8 and Section 22.4-3.\n\n0.5.5 Election of Registered Series.\n\nThe Executive Director may, at any time and on a per-Series basis, elect to establish a Series as a "registered series" under § 18-218 of the LLC Act, or to convert an existing protected Series to a registered Series. Any such election shall be (a) recorded as an attribute of the Certificate of Establishment of the Series, (b) implemented by the filing of the certificate of registered series with the Secretary of State as required by § 18-218(c) of the LLC Act, and (c) accompanied by payment of the per-Series annual fee specified in § 18-1107 of the LLC Act. A registered series under § 18-218 enjoys the limitation of liability set forth in § 18-218(b), which parallels the limitation set forth in Section 1.8.2 for protected series under § 18-215(b).',
